34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The complaint log shows nine unresolved conflicts. The neighbouring block’s charge caused two households to stop attending meetings. We must avoid creating a system that alienates residents.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Wow, nine conflicts! That’s a lot. But my morning watch showed four people shifting bikes just to leave. We need to fix the flow!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The eaves row stays dry; beyond the downpipe, saddles remain wet. The station park costs 2,600 yen monthly, with fourteen households already waiting.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The ledger is empty. Capital work means a levy. The handover file shows three hours monthly just to reconcile cash. We are broke, and billing adds more work.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The minutes show no review in five years. The frame needs greasing twice yearly. We need a system that doesn’t quietly collapse.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, your financials confirm the risk. @Toshio, the lack of review explains the decay. We need a zero-cost, low-maintenance solution to prevent further alienation.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, fourteen people waiting outside is scary! @Shunichi, I’m sorry we’re broke. I just want a fair, simple way for everyone to leave without shifting bikes!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, external options are saturated. @Shunichi, capital levies are unviable. We must optimize the existing dry row to minimize morning friction and rain damage.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, “optimize” is a polite word for doing nothing. @Toshio, if we can’t afford the levy, we can’t afford the frame. We’re stuck with the status quo.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the frame is optional. The real cost is the unrecorded labor. We need a rotation, not a permanent burden.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, rotation is the answer. It distributes the burden so no one feels targeted. @Shunichi, this costs nothing but prevents the social decay I saw in the logs.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, rotation sounds great! But my sticker data shows people want to pay for priority. Can we mix a small fee with rotation?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, fees contradict the financial reality. @Toshio, rotation is logical, but we must prioritize the dry row to prevent asset degradation.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, people want to pay? The ledger says we can’t afford to collect it. @Toshio, rotation is just unpaid labor. I’m not volunteering for that.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, it’s not unpaid labor; it’s shared responsibility. The greasing takes minutes, not hours. We just need a schedule that doesn’t vanish.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the neighbouring block proves fees destroy community. @Toshio, a simple rotation prevents the isolation I saw. We must choose stability over convenience.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Shunichi, I get it! But my data shows people *want* to pay for priority. Maybe a tiny fee helps? @Toshio, rotation is good, but let’s keep it simple!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the ledger is empty, but the rain is not. I propose a strict rotation for the dry row. It costs nothing, preserves the bikes, and eliminates the morning shoving match.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, “strict” is doing heavy lifting. If the ledger is empty, who enforces it? I’m not paying for the privilege of being ignored.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, enforcement is the problem. I propose a rotating custodian. One person per month handles the greasing and checks. No permanent burden, no hidden costs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
