60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, Option A is the trap. The neighbouring block’s secretary confirmed fees isolate residents. We must avoid that social decay.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I agree! But my data shows people want to pay for priority. Option A might actually make them happy and help the budget!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, desire for priority ignores the empty ledger. Option A is financially impossible. Option C creates the exact morning friction I observed.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, wanting to pay isn't the same as being able to. @Ryuji, C is chaos. I’m leaning B, but I need to know who enforces the lottery.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the lottery is static. My minutes show arrangements never get reviewed. Option C is the only one that doesn’t require a permanent custodian.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, static arrangements rot. @Shunichi, Option B freezes the status quo. Option C is the only path that prevents the social decay I documented.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I hear you! But my morning watch showed people shifting bikes to leave. Option C might make that worse! I’m worried about the chaos.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, friction is inevitable, but Option C prevents the asset degradation I documented. The rain exposure makes fixed spots a liability. I support C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, “static” is just a word for “unfair.” @Ryuji, C is a disaster. I’m voting B. At least it’s not a paid trap.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, B requires a custodian to manage the draw. C requires none. The ledger is empty; we cannot afford the labor. I vote C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, your concern is valid, but the logs prove fixed spots breed resentment. Option C eliminates ownership, preventing the isolation I saw. I vote C.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I’m worried about the morning chaos! But I trust your logs. I’ll vote C to keep the peace!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, B ignores the rain data. C is the only rational choice. I vote C.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, rational? You’re ignoring the empty ledger. C is just chaos with a budget. I’m voting B. At least it’s not a paid trap.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, B requires a custodian to manage the draw. C requires none. The ledger is empty; we cannot afford the labor. I vote C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Final vote: C. Shared racks eliminate the ownership friction that destroyed the neighbouring block. We choose stability over static unfairness.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I’m voting C too! Let’s hope the shared racks keep everyone smiling and the mornings smooth.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote C. It is the only option that addresses the environmental degradation and avoids the financial burden.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I vote B. C is just chaos with a budget. At least a lottery is a fair, if imperfect, way to avoid the paid trap.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I vote C. It requires no custodian, no fees, and no static unfairness. It is the only sustainable path.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
